<title>UK: Shell says Nigerian villagers to free injured staff.</title>
<headline>Shell says Nigerian villagers to free injured staff.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil giant Shell said on Monday Nigerian villagers had agreed to release six members of staff injured when oil installations in the Niger delta were occupied over the weekend.</p>
<p>The Shell staff, hurt when community groups overran flow stations in the northern swamp region to gain publicity over a local government dispute, would be transported back to the nearby town of Warri on Tuesday morning, the company said in London.</p>
</text>
